# NOTE(host-dependent): system-timezone returns the host's IANA tz id (§3.8),
# which is host-dependent and has no deterministic literal output. The only
# stable, spec-grounded property is that its result is a resolvable IANA
# identifier — i.e. round-tripping it through time/timezone does not raise
# CXER3302. The rendered timezone element (name/offset/dst) still varies by
# host, so this asserts only the round-trip succeeds via timezone-offset being
# an int; reconcile once a $mock/CX_TZ_DIR-pinned harness exists for a
# deterministic host tz. (Host-dependence of system-timezone is declared in
# README.md "Reference platform — POSIX"; this case's assertion stays as the
# stable round-trip property.)
 [case id=time-107-system-timezone-resolvable level=core
  [tags time source system-timezone deterministic]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[>= [$time:timezone-offset [$time:datetime-with-tz 2026 1 15 12 0 0 [$time:system-timezone]]] -86400]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER0271
#]]
 ]

 # Wall-clock reads require the `clock` capability (§8). Under the empty-cap
 # runner they raise CXER0271; behavior (a plausible datetime/date/instant)
 # belongs in a clock-granted / $mock harness.
 [case id=time-108-now-cap-denied level=core
